* The bog's bed (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script; owner,
* 2026-11-11: things kept getting down below the bog). Run by openc2e after
* the world loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* The bog under the swamp walkway (room 43, water, x 4800-5700) is painted
* about 45 px deep: its surface is the walkway's line (y 2295) and its bed
* lies at about y 2337-2340, rising to the surface at both banks. The room
* went down to y 2399 with no floor line, so whatever sank came to rest up to
* 60 px inside the painted earth (an old norn, a beach ball). Its floor line
* now follows the bed, traced from the picture every 10 px (heights above
* the room's bottom, y 2399).
* At both ends the walkway climbs onto dry banks (room 44's line rises to
* y 2255 at x 4800 and 5700) and the painted water stops short (about x
* 4895 and 5690). There the bed lies flush with the water's surface: a bed
* traced under the banks (first version, the same day) lay a little below
* the walkway's slope inside the painted earth, and a norn walking down the
* west bank was set on it, half buried.
ssfc 43 12 0 104 95 104 130 69 160 57 250 62 400 59 650 63 720 75 820 65 860 85 890 104 900 104
* creatures caught under a bank: back onto the dry ground beside it
enum 4 0 0
  doif posb gt 2296 and posb lt 2420 and posx gt 4760 and posx lt 4900
    mvto 4650 2150
    setv vely 1
  endi
  doif posb gt 2296 and posb lt 2420 and posx gt 5680 and posx lt 5800
    mvto 5760 2150
    setv vely 1
  endi
next
*
* Creatures stuck in the water under the walkway (owner's screenshot,
* 2026-11-14: one below the walkway, only its feet showing). The walkway
* (room 44, floor line 2255 at the banks, 2285 in the middle) lies just over
* the water (room 43, surface 2295), and the way between them was open, so a
* creature could drop through into the water. There it walked along the bed
* and up a bank to the surface, where it stood 20-40 px under the walkway's
* floor at the bank, could not step up onto it, and could go no further (the
* water's sides are closed): tested on a copy, a creature put in the water
* ended pacing under the west bank (x 4787-4896, feet 2295) for good. The
* check above runs only at load (and missed feet at exactly 2295).
* - The way from the walkway down into the water is closed, so nothing
*   drops in.
* - A watcher (2 1 159, invisible, every 2 s, all in one tick) sets any
*   creature in the water back on the walkway right above it, its feet on
*   the walkway's floor line at its middle (moved by script, so not a fall).
setv door 0 43 44 0
enum 2 1 159 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 159 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1330 tick 20 slow
scrp 2 1 159 9
  inst
  enum 4 0 0
    doif posx gt 4800 and posx lt 5700 and posb gt 2290 and posb lt 2420
*     the walkway's floor at x (room 44's floor points, heights above 2295:
*     40 at 4800, 20 at 5000, 10 at 5250, 20 at 5450, 40 at 5700)
      setv var0 posx
      subv var0 4800
      doif var0 lt 200
        setv var1 var0
        mulv var1 20
        divv var1 200
        setv var2 40
        subv var2 var1
      else
        doif var0 lt 450
          setv var1 var0
          subv var1 200
          mulv var1 10
          divv var1 250
          setv var2 20
          subv var2 var1
        else
          doif var0 lt 650
            setv var1 var0
            subv var1 450
            mulv var1 10
            divv var1 200
            setv var2 10
            addv var2 var1
          else
            setv var1 var0
            subv var1 650
            mulv var1 20
            divv var1 250
            setv var2 20
            addv var2 var1
          endi
        endi
      endi
      setv var3 2295
      subv var3 var2
      setv var4 posb
      subv var4 post
      subv var3 var4
      mvto posl var3
      setv velx 0
      setv vely 0
    endi
  next
endm
